wxWidgets 3.2.12 generic wxRegion: Subtract() took the wrong difference and
changed shared data. DoSubtract() passed (region, this) to XSubtractRegion,
whose arguments are (minuend, subtrahend, result), so this.Subtract(rect)
became rect minus this: empty when rect lies inside this. It also skipped
AllocExclusive(), so every copy sharing the data (a paint's update region
and its copies) was emptied too. OpenCPN's chart canvas copies its update
region, subtracts the chart bar, then blits the copy: nothing was drawn.

--- a/src/generic/regiong.cpp
+++ b/src/generic/regiong.cpp
@@ -355,7 +355,12 @@
         return true;
     }
 
-    return REGION::XSubtractRegion(M_REGIONDATA_OF(region),M_REGIONDATA,M_REGIONDATA);
+    // this minus region, on our own copy of the data: the arguments were the
+    // wrong way round (region minus this, empty for a rectangle inside this)
+    // and the data shared with other copies (a paint's update region) was
+    // changed as well
+    AllocExclusive();
+    return REGION::XSubtractRegion(M_REGIONDATA,M_REGIONDATA_OF(region),M_REGIONDATA);
 }
 
 bool wxRegionGeneric::DoXor(const wxRegion& region)
